Full Stack Engineer Take-Home Assessment

Objective
Design and develop a full-stack web application that consumes publicly available data
from data.gov.sg.

High-Level Requirements
The solution should:
 Retrieve and integrate data from any dataset of your choice available on data.gov.sg.
 Present the data through a clear and user-friendly interface.
 Provide appropriate capabilities for users to explore and interact with the data.
 Analyse the selected dataset and present meaningful summaries or insights derived from
the data (Optional).
 Demonstrate sound frontend and backend application design.
 Provide Infrastructure as Code (IaC) that defines the AWS infrastructure required to
deploy and operate the solution.
 Include appropriate automated testing and supporting technical documentation.
Candidates are free to select the technology stack, application architecture, AWS services, and
implementation approach.
Deployment to AWS is not required; however, the application must run successfully in a local
environment.

Assessment Criteria
The assessment will focus on the overall quality of the solution, engineering practices, technical
decision-making, and the candidate’s ability to explain and justify their design choices,
assumptions, and trade-offs.

Submission
The completed assessment should be submitted within three calendar days from the date it is
provided.
The complete source code, Infrastructure as Code, automated tests, and README
documentation should be maintained in a Git repository.
Please provide access to the repository for review as part of your submission.
